fastpath-leapquant
Copyright 2026 FastPathLabs

This product is an independent implementation of the LeapQuant method described in:
Y. Pan, H. Xi, K. Zhu, et al. "LeapQuant: Efficient Linear Attention with Accurate
Recurrent State Quantization." arXiv:2609.38166, 2026. https://leapquant.github.io

The method is the work of its authors. The code in this repository was written by
FastPathLabs from the paper, with these exceptions:

- kernel/leapquant_triton.py: the structure of the decode kernel is adapted from
  SGLang's fused_recurrent_linear_replayssm_decode_kernel
  (sglang/kernels/ops/attention/linear/fused_recurrent_linear_replayssm.py),
  Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2023-2024 SGLang Team. SGLang ported that kernel
  from vLLM's ReplaySSM kernel (Apache License 2.0, Copyright contributors to the
  vLLM project). The changes are described in the file's header.

- eval/lcb_sandbox_runner.py and eval/lcb_sandbox.py: contain grading code, prompt
  constants, the question template and the code extraction copied from LiveCodeBench
  (github.com/LiveCodeBench/LiveCodeBench, commit 28fef95e), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2024 LiveCodeBench. The MIT license text is reproduced in both files.

- integrations/sglang/*.patch and integrations/vllm/*.patch: patches against SGLang
  and vLLM (both Apache License 2.0). The context lines in them are SGLang and vLLM code.
